      "output": "## The far city: eight models, handed on unchanged\n\nAll eight files were read by one standard-library Python script (`inspect_glb.py`), copied byte for byte to their own names and published. Every publish receipt's SHA-256 equals the one the script computed and the one supplied with the task.\n\n| File | Bytes | Meshes | Triangles | Materials | Textures (embedded WebP: colour / ORM / normal bytes) | Size in metres, x × y × z | SHA-256 (first 12) | Same bytes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| hotel-peach-far.glb | 172,508 | 1 | 5,546 | 1 | 3 at 256 px: 14,076 / 14,808 / 1,090 | 0.826 × 0.947 × 0.998 | `45d6cb61519f` | same bytes: yes |\n| hotel-coral-far.glb | 140,920 | 1 | 4,075 | 1 | 3 at 256 px: 11,038 / 19,208 / 1,550 | 0.996 × 0.646 × 0.668 | `73027d96319a` | same bytes: yes |\n| hotel-lemon-far.glb | 151,556 | 1 | 4,658 | 1 | 3 at 256 px: 12,390 / 15,854 / 1,994 | 0.584 × 0.928 × 0.998 | `dd1b01a83811` | same bytes: yes |\n| hotel-white-far.glb | 140,500 | 1 | 4,192 | 1 | 3 at 256 px: 17,084 / 13,854 / 1,030 | 0.840 × 0.998 × 0.830 | `0d37dddc1e5c` | same bytes: yes |\n| hotel-mint-far.glb | 139,844 | 1 | 4,756 | 1 | 3 at 256 px: 11,554 / 9,008 / 1,624 | 0.785 × 0.723 × 0.998 | `344d40d8085b` | same bytes: yes |\n| hotel-aqua-far.glb | 157,504 | 1 | 5,637 | 1 | 3 at 256 px: 1,266 / 17,718 / 350 | 0.994 × 0.647 × 0.994 | `5d15017978b5` | same bytes: yes |\n| tower-c.glb | 141,268 | 1 | 2,279 | 1 | 3 at 512 px: 39,814 / 4,416 / 34,444 | 0.385 × 0.998 × 0.666 | `45feae44d55c` | same bytes: yes |\n| lifeguard-hut.glb | 142,144 | 1 | 2,811 | 1 | 3 at 512 px: 26,520 / 41,232 / 6,120 | 0.998 × 0.596 × 0.572 | `39bb3d0de284` | same bytes: yes |\n\nTotals: 1,186,244 bytes and 33,954 triangles.\n\n- **Triangles** are each primitive's index accessor count divided by 3; every count divides evenly. Each file has one mesh with one primitive.\n- **Size** is the POSITION accessor's min and max taken through the node's scale and translation. The positions are 16-bit normalised integers, so the script divides them by 32767 first. Each node scales by about 0.497 to 0.499; the unscaled accessor box is about 2 units on its longest side.\n- **Compression** (`extensionsUsed`, and all three are also in `extensionsRequired`, in every file): `EXT_meshopt_compression`, `EXT_texture_webp`, `KHR_mesh_quantization`.\n- **Materials** are one per file: double-sided, opaque, with colour, metal-roughness and normal texture slots and no colour factor.\n- **Not checked:** the compressed geometry was not decoded and no model was rendered or looked at; the standard library has no decoder for it. The files hold no animation and no sound.\n\n**For the builders.** No file is far larger than the others; the largest, hotel-peach-far.glb, is about 1.2 times the smallest. Four things are worth knowing:\n\n- **Loader:** it needs a meshopt decoder and WebP texture support, because all eight files require those extensions.\n- **Scale and placement:** every model fits a box about 1 m on its longest side, centred on the origin, so the base sits near y = −0.3 to −0.5, not at 0. The game has to scale and lift each one. tower-c is also off-centre in x (−0.134 to 0.251).\n- **Proportions:** coral and aqua are wider than tall (y about 0.65). Peach, lemon and mint have their longest side on z, not y.\n- **hotel-aqua-far.glb is close to having no colour texture:** its colour image is 1,266 bytes. A separate Pillow pass (outside the standard-library script) found it an almost flat neutral grey, mean RGB 170, 172, 171 with a spread of 2, and its normal map flat too (350 bytes). Its aqua colour, if it has one in the game, must come from the game's code. The other seven colour images vary normally.",
