      "output": "## People and the sky: 7 files, handed on unchanged\n\n| File | Bytes | What it is | Measures | SHA-256 (first 12) | Same bytes |\n|---|---:|---|---|---|---|\n| ines.glb | 1,354,124 | Ines, rigged person (the player on foot) | 23 bones, 1 mesh, 11,526 triangles; clips: idle 15.367 s, run 1.267 s, walk 2.367 s | `b54a43d823a5` | same bytes: yes |\n| ped-woman.glb | 1,258,992 | Passer-by (woman), rigged | 23 bones, 1 mesh, 8,736 triangles; clips: sit 7.2 s, standing_relax 17.6 s, walk 2.367 s | `88cc79d112ba` | same bytes: yes |\n| ped-man.glb | 1,232,940 | Passer-by (man), rigged | 23 bones, 1 mesh, 8,258 triangles; clips: sit 7.2 s, standing_relax 17.6 s, walk 2.367 s | `8ff5c296bf00` | same bytes: yes |\n| pano.jpg | 407,936 | Painted sky, sunset | 4096 × 1738 px, RGB JPEG | `21b89667bc37` | same bytes: yes |\n| dusk.jpg | 214,437 | Painted sky, dusk | 4096 × 1738 px, RGB JPEG | `8bbb86d81c3c` | same bytes: yes |\n| frond.webp | 205,956 | Palm frond, cut out | 512 × 1024 px, RGBA WebP; has alpha: yes (29.1 % of pixels fully transparent, 63.6 % fully opaque) | `4e633733f82d` | same bytes: yes |\n| bark.jpg | 178,192 | Palm bark | 512 × 918 px, RGB JPEG | `23b8eb4cc3e3` | same bytes: yes |\n\nTotal: 4,852,577 bytes.\n\n**What the two skies show** (each viewed once with workspace_view; both returned a picture):\n- pano.jpg: a small sun disc with a halo sits low at centre above a hazy orange horizon band, with pink cumulus on either side and a field of small pink-orange cloudlets on violet-blue sky above.\n- dusk.jpg: the sun is gone; a magenta-pink glow lies along the horizon under dark purple cloud streaks with pink undersides, with cumulus towers low at left and right, a deep blue upper sky with a few faint stars, and a dark strip along the bottom edge.\n\n**Checks that ran:**\n- One script (`look.py`, standard library plus Pillow) read all 7 files and computed each SHA-256; all 7 equal the hashes supplied with the task.\n- Each file was copied to its own name, and the copy's hash equalled the source's.\n- All 7 publish receipts returned the same SHA-256 as step 1, so no file needed a second copy or publish.\n- The models were measured from the GLB's JSON only; nothing was loaded in an engine or played. frond.webp and bark.jpg were measured but not viewed.\n\n**For the builders:**\n- **WebP textures required:** all three models list `EXT_texture_webp` under extensionsRequired, so the loader must decode WebP textures. No other extension is used. Each model has 1 material with a base-colour texture and 3 embedded WebP images, so none is untextured.\n- **Clip names differ:** Ines has idle, run and walk; the passers-by have sit, standing_relax and walk. The passers-by have no clip named \"idle\" (their standing clip is standing_relax) and no run; walk is 2.367 s in all three.\n- **Sky shape:** both skies are 4096 × 1738, about 2.36:1, not the 2:1 of a full equirectangular sphere, so they should be mapped as a panoramic band or partial dome.\n- **Bark size:** bark.jpg is 512 × 918; its height is not a power of two, which matters only if it is to tile with mipmaps on a strict pipeline.\n- **Sizes:** the three models are 3,846,056 of the 4,852,577 bytes; no single file is far larger than its kind.\n- **Sound:** there is none in this set.",
